''See the [https://wiki.project1999.com/Ring_8_player_agreement Ring 8 Server Roll] for the current Ring 8 Server Roll times.''

''This is the 8th quest in Garadain's series. It involves an all-out war against Chief Ry'Gorr and his troops.''

'''This quest is challenging, and you only get ONE chance to complete it successfully. Once you hand your ring to Garadain, you must give the Marching Orders to Lady Gloradin (who has a 24-hour respawn timer). The siege on the orc fort will begin immediately afterward. Your goal is to kill [[Chief Ry`Gorr]], loot his head, and deliver it to Garadain. It's crucial to keep Garadain alive, as he only accepts the head during the event—and only after he shouts "CHARGE!" Note that Chief Ry'Gorr will only drop his head during this specific event.'''

''The preferred strategy is as follows: You’ll need a group of 2-6 players, levels 55-60, to handle this event comfortably. Before handing in the Marching Orders, have your party members cast invisibility and enter the Ry'Gorr fort. After entering through the main entrance, turn right and proceed to a relatively open, safe area away from enemy mobs. **Ensure Garadain is alive** before you hand in the Marching Orders to [[Gloradin Coldheart]]. 

''Once the Marching Orders are handed in, the event starts, and there is no way to stop it. Failing here means you must begin the Coldain Ring quest series from the very first ring! [[Garadain Glacierbane]] will begin marching towards the Ry'Gorr fort, accompanied by a small dwarven army. After you’ve handed in the orders, invis up and join your group inside the fort. Your objective is to kill the special version of [[Chief Ry`Gorr]] that spawns, loot his head, and hand it in to Garadain AFTER he shouts "CHARGE!" but BEFORE the dwarves storm the fort.''

''A minute or two after you hand in the Marching Orders, the special version of Chief Ry'Gorr spawns near the fort's entrance, accompanied by several giant guards and orc allies. At this point, pull the Chief and kill him as quickly as possible. You can use Lull/Harmony to avoid pulling the giants, but the Oracle standing next to the Chief will aggro regardless. However, the Oracle can be pacified. The Chief, his pet Firbrand, and possibly the Oracle will come when you aggro the Chief. Focus on killing him quickly and loot his head. The Chief isn’t particularly resistant to spells, can be slowed, and has relatively few hit points. A group of 2 or 3 level 60 players, with at least one healer and one DPS, can handle this easily.''

''Once you have the Chief's head, invis up and exit the fort through the main entrance, heading north. You’ll find Garadain and a small army of dwarf archers and soldiers overlooking the Ry'Gorr fort. If you’ve been quick, you’ll arrive while Garadain is giving his pep talk to the troops. DO NOT hand him the Chief’s head at this point. If you do, you’ll lose the head and fail the quest. Wait until Garadain finishes speaking and begins marching toward the fort. When he shouts "CHARGE," that’s your signal to hand in the head. There’s no need to worry about him despawning or resetting—the "CHARGE" shout is your green light. Once you hand in the head, you will receive the 8th ring.''

''This method allows you to avoid participating in the large battle that follows. If Garadain reaches the fort and engages in combat, he could die, which would result in failure. By completing the hand-in before the battle begins, you can avoid this risk entirely.''

